# Leaf spec: shaft tool props and progression geometry (producer)

Objective: build the illustrative shaper cutter and hob props from the certified clearance-v4 dimensions, and the closed-form machining progression that turns the finished CAD shaft meshes into the blank/partial/finished states without CSG.

Context (read, do not modify): docs/jgun-manufacturing-inspection-plan.md sections 2 and 4 (owner storyline: shaper cuts, slow exit macro, recap, material cards, revised blank, hobbing, supports, finale); project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/camera/clearance-v4/README.md and report.json (CERTIFIED illustrative tool dimensions and paths; use these numbers exactly); src/scene/inspection/shaft/story.ts (shaftBeats authored table, 43 s) and shaft/script.ts (cards/stress timing; cool scan starts 32.8 s, so hob withdrawal must be complete by 32.0 s); src/scene/inspection/timeline.ts (closed-form allocation-free sampler style with caller-owned out objects); src/scene/inspection/story.ts (StoryRuntime interfaces). Shaft-local frame: +Y is the shaft axis in millimetres in CAD; the runtime GLB (public/models/manufacturing-core-full.glb, nodes legacyshaft/approvedshaft/housing/legacybearing/legacyring/approvedbearing/approvedring) is metres with shaft-local +Y exported to glTF -Z (one conversion only). Measured: 10 teeth, 36 deg pitch, tip r 6.0834, root r 4.2918, face y 3.1749..9.5249, legacy last tooth material y 9.875, legacy groove floor r 3.97 at y 10.41, groove wall y 10.94; approved ramp floor ends y 13.78 at filler OD 6.074; approved journal r 6.325 from y 14.18.
Rules: you are not alone in the codebase; never revert or stage others' work; no git operations; do not read TODO.md or queue docs (this spec is complete). Everything must be a pure function of time (no accumulators, no Math.random/Date/performance), allocation-free in per-frame paths, deterministic under any seek order. Do not register stories, mount components or edit shared scene files.

Files you own (create only): scripts/manufacturing/cutter_outline.mjs, src/scene/inspection/shaft/cutterOutline.json (generated), src/scene/inspection/shaft/toolSpec.ts, src/scene/inspection/shaft/tools.ts, src/scene/inspection/shaft/progression.ts, src/scene/inspection/shaft/progression.test.ts, src/scene/inspection/shaft/tools.test.ts, project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/gates/shaft-tools-progression.md.

1. cutter_outline.mjs (Node, no deps): read project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/camera/profile-study.json profiles.legacy["6.0"] (7200 work polar radii at 0.05 deg; work outline r(phi)). Compute the conjugate disc-cutter outline for N=20 teeth at centre distance 15.5 mm, signed ratio work/cutter -2, by the envelope method: for roll angles over one cutter pitch at <=0.02 deg, transform the work outline into the cutter frame and take, per cutter polar bin (<=0.05 deg), the minimum radius occupied by work material; clamp tips at 11.2032 mm (clearance-v4 tip) and roots at 15.5 - 6.0834 - 0.15 mm; leave 0.005 mm stock. Emit one tooth (18 deg) as a polyline of [angle_rad, radius_mm] with <=360 points plus metadata (sha256 of profile-study.json, parameters). Write cutterOutline.json. Print max deviation of the outline vs the matched_shaper_diagnostics in profile-study.json if comparable.
2. toolSpec.ts: frozen constants copied from clearance-v4 report.json (shaper: teeth 20, centre 15.5, tip 11.2032, thickness 1.2, stroke centre y range, overtravel 0.5, backoff 2.0, hub r8 l6, clamp r9 l3, arbor r7 l12; hob: R 5.87, normal module 1, starts 1, lead angle 5.5587 deg, length 16, centre distance at depth (root + R), stop yc 9.5249, infeed yc -4.195, retract 2.5, collars r R+1 w3, arbor r R-1.5 l12) and the report path; test that they match report.json values.
3. tools.ts: buildShaperCutter(): THREE.ExtrudeGeometry (depth 1.2 mm, scaled to metres) from the 20-tooth outline, plus hub/clamp/arbor cylinders, steel material instances supplied by caller; returns { root: Group, cuttingEdgeLocal: Vector3 (rake face point at the tip on the leading face), dispose }. buildHob(): body cylinder at root of thread, 10 gashes, single-start helical thread approximated by trapezoid tooth instances (InstancedMesh) placed along the helix with lead = pi*m/cos(lead angle), outside radius R, plus collars/arbor; returns { root, dispose }. Geometry in metres, axes documented (cutter axis parallel to shaft axis; hob axis perpendicular, tilted by lead angle). Keep triangle counts modest (cutter <= 12k, hob <= 20k) and report them in tests.
4. progression.ts: closed-form state and shader patch.
   - type ProgressionState = { mode: 'none'|'shaping'|'hobbing'; spaceDepth: Float32Array(10) in [0,1]; engagedSpace: number (-1 none); edgeY: number (mm, cutter leading face during the current stroke; behind it the engaged space has its new depth, ahead the previous depth); hobYc: number (mm); hobA: number (mm centre distance); hobR: number }.
   - progressedRadius(r, y, azimuth, state, shaft: 'legacy'|'approved'): CPU mirror. For legacy shaping, only vertices with FACE_START<=y<=9.875 and r < OD are affected: r' = min(OD, r + (1 - depth_i)*(OD - ROOT)) where i is the tooth-space index from azimuth (clock: measure from the mesh; expose SPACE_CLOCK_RAD constant and a test that recovers it from approved/legacy vertex data you can load in tests via the GLB? if loading the GLB in vitest is impractical, derive the clock from profile-study.json legacy 6.0 polar data instead). For approved hobbing: affected band FACE_START<=y<=13.78: floor(y) = root for y <= hobYc; A - sqrt(R^2 - (y - hobYc)^2) for hobYc < y < hobYc + R; OD beyond; r' = max(r, min(OD, floor(y))). Use the authored untilted circle R=6.0 with centre root+6.0 at final yc 9.5249 for the visual floor so the final state equals the approved mesh; state that R 5.87 tilted is the certified tool and R 6.0 untilted is its equivalent meridian floor (clearance-v4 ramp fit).
   - applyProgression(material: MeshStandardMaterial | MeshPhysicalMaterial, uniforms): onBeforeCompile patch adding the same law in the vertex shader (shaft-local coordinates via an attribute-free position transform: pass a uniform matrix from object space to shaft-local mm), with normals blended toward radial where clamped to OD. Also add stress overlay uniforms (kind none/warm/cool, mix, scanProgress, band yMin/yMax, rMax) producing a localized warm (red-orange) or cool (green-blue) tint that keeps metallic edges (mix into emissive/diffuse lightly, not replace).
   - Tests: final shaping state (all depths 1) leaves every sample r unchanged; depth 0 puts every face-band sample at OD and leaves the groove (y>9.875) unchanged; hobbing at final yc reproduces approved floor samples within 0.01 mm (use profile-study approved polar data at y 9.72, 10.92, 13.78 if available); monotonic in depth and yc; allocation-free; shader string contains the patch markers.

Verification: node scripts/manufacturing/cutter_outline.mjs; npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft; npm run typecheck. Gate file lists A1 outline derived and bounded, A2 constants equal report, A3 props built within triangle budgets, A4 progression law tests, A5 typecheck/tests pass. Report changed paths, commands, results, unresolved items.
